==Notes==
*If [[Luxon]]s control an outpost listed above, five Kurzick Guards will be killed by the [[Luxon Guard]]s when an instance of the outpost is created, leaving their [[corpse]]s outside the outpost's [[portal]].
*Like Kurzick Priests, the Kurzick Guards at a Resurrection Shrine determine their attitude towards the party the first time a player enters compass range, and will not change it even if the party's unspent faction totals change.
**Only guards that are friendly to the party when first approached will attack foes that enter their aggro range.
**It is possible for the guard's attitude to differ from those of the other shrine [[Non-player character|NPCs]]. If a guard's attitude is friendly, and the priest is challenged to a fight for the portal, the guard will not turn hostile, will fight the other shrine NPCs, and will not prevent the shrine from being activated.

